4. Assess real demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) the 3-month average volume BEFORE the spike month vs the spike month, (b) the 3-month average volume AFTER the spike month (if available), (c) the return rate trend (spike month vs surrounding months). Save these diagnostic metrics to offline_data/anomaly_diagnostics.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded data: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/volume_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing the top-3 anomalies with region, product, month, volume, 24-month mean, ratio, return rate; (3) every key number must carry an inline source annotation in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）' for derived ratios; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike looks like real demand or channel stuffing, citing the diagnostic metrics; (5) all data sourced exclusively from the local CSV, no web data. Embed the diagnostic tables as Markdown tables in the report → code_agent
